# ==============================================================================
# Multi-block structured meshing (MESH_MODE 1) — an EIGHT-BLOCK TWO-RING O-GRID
# around a 2:1 ELLIPSE, whose middle ring is DECLARED rather than drawn.
#
#   ./run.sh -conf config/multiblock_tworing_curve.dat
#
# This is issue #175's case, and it is deliberately one declaration away from
# config/multiblock_tworing_offset.dat beside it. That case's seam edges declare
# `follows` on a THIRD geometry file, examples/geometries/ellipse_offset.dat,
# written by the GUI's offset service. These declare the curve they ARE:
#
#   "curve": {"kind": "ellipse", "centre": [0, 0], "a": 0.75, "b": 0.5}
#
# So this file names TWO geometries where that one names three, and the seam has
# no file, no sidecar, no segment id and no faceting.
#
# WHAT THAT COSTS, STATED HERE RATHER THAN DISCOVERED LATER. A concentric ellipse
# is not an ellipse's offset. Measured in #154: this curve sits 0.241523 from the
# body at the nose where a constant ring would be 0.250000, so the ring is 3.39%
# thin in the one place the boundary layer is thickest. The offset case still
# ships, and still wants its file. Both numbers are in docs/design_notes/mesher.md.
#
# THE BUDGET IS THE SHIPPED O-GRIDS' — 4704 vertices, 9216 triangles, 192
# boundary edges — so the two two-ring cases are comparable cell for cell.
# ==============================================================================

MESH_MODE 1
MESH_TOPOLOGY_FILE examples/topology/tworing_curve.json

# TWO geometries, and both of them are boundaries. The middle ring is not here
# because it is not a file: it is four edges of the topology document.
GEOM_FILE examples/geometries/ellipse_body.dat
GEOM_FILE examples/geometries/ellipse_farfield.dat

# The wall spacing, under the name it already has. Only the INNER ring's radials
# take it; the outer ring's first cell is declared in the topology document,
# because the seam is not a wall.
BL_INITIAL_THICKNESS 0.001

MB_SPLIT_QUADS 1

# The FALLBACK. Both geometries bind, so nothing should reach it.
BC_GEOM wall

EXPORT_VTK 1
EXPORT_STARCD 1
OUTPUT_FILENAME results/meshes/multiblock_tworing_curve/mesh_multiblock_tworing_curve.vtk
